slash, aFilename!helpDir fileExists: aFilename!ScratchPlugin primOpenURL: helpDir pathName, FileDirectory slash, aFilename!helpDir fileExists: aFilename!helpDir fileExists: aFilename!ScratchPlugin primOpenURL: helpDir pathName, FileDirectory slash, aFilename!ScratchPlugin primOpenURL: helpDir pathName, FileDirectory slash, aFilename!helpDir!self fileNames!!InputSensor commentStamp: 'jm 2/19/2009 13:06' prior: 35341406!I represent an interface to the user input devices. There is one instance of me in the system, named Sensor.I support two alternate ways to get user inputs from the VM:  a. state based, using primMousePt, primMouseButtons, primKbdPeek, and primKbdNext  b. event based, using primGetNextEvent:The method useOSEvents: sets which technique I use. Squeak images and VMs before version 3.1 use and support only (a).When using (b), I record the most recent cursor position and the state of the mouse buttons and modifier keys in  instance variables. I also keep a queue of unprocessed events and an array of flags that record the up/down state of every key, indexed by the ascii value of the key. When using (a) these instance variables are not used and are set to nil.Event Types:  0 - null event  1 - mouse event  2.- key event  3 - file drag-drop event  4 - menu event  5 - window eventNull event=============The Null event is returned when Smalltalk asks for more events but none are available.[1]		- event type = 0[2-8]	- unusedMouse event===============[1]	- event type = 1[2]	- time stamp[3]	- mouse x position[4]	- mouse y position[5]	- button state; bitfield with the following entries:		1	-	yellow (e.g., right) button		2	-	blue (e.g., middle) button		4	-	red (e.g., left) button		[all other bits are currently undefined][6]	- modifier keys; bitfield with the following entries:		1	-	shift key		2	-	ctrl key		4	-	(Mac specific) option key		8	-	Cmd/Alt key		[all other bits are currently undefined][7]	- unused[8]	- unusedKeyboard event===================[1]	- event type = 2[2]	- time stamp[3]	- character code		For now the character code is in Mac Roman encoding.[4]	- press state; integer with the following meaning		0	-	character		1	-	key press (down)		2	- 	key release (up)[5]	- modifier keys (same as in mouse events)[6]	- unused[7]	- unused[8]	- unusedFile Drag-Drop event========================[1]	- event type = 3[2]	- time stamp[3]	- subtype	1	- drag enter	2	- drag move	3	- drag leave	4	- file drop	5	- drag to another window[4]	- drop position x[5]	- drop position y[6]	- modifier bits[7]	- file count[8]	- unusedMenu event===============[1]	- event type = 4[2]	- time stamp[3]	- menu ID[4]	- item ID[5]	- unused?[6]	- unused?[7]	- unused?[8]	- window IDWindow event=================[1]	- event type = 5[2]	- time stamp[3]	- window subtype	1	- geometry change; details in fields 4-7	2	- close	3	- iconize	4	- activate	5	- redraw[4]	- window left[5]	- window top[6]	- window width[7]	- window height[8]	- window ID!!InputSensor commentStamp: 'jm 2/19/2009 13:06' prior: 40204924!I represent an interface to the user input devices. There is one instance of me in the system, named Sensor.I support two alternate ways to get user inputs from the VM:  a. state based, using primMousePt, primMouseButtons, primKbdPeek, and primKbdNext  b. event based, using primGetNextEvent:The method useOSEvents: sets which technique I use. Squeak images and VMs before version 3.1 use and support only (a).When using (b), I record the most recent cursor position and the state of the mouse buttons and modifier keys in  instance variables. I also keep a queue of unprocessed events and an array of flags that record the up/down state of every key, indexed by the ascii value of the key. When using (a) these instance variables are not used and are set to nil.Event Types:  0 - null event  1 - mouse event  2.- key event  3 - file drag-drop event  4 - menu event  5 - window eventNull event=============The Null event is returned when Smalltalk asks for more events but none are available.[1]		- event type = 0[2-8]	- unusedMouse event===============[1]	- event type = 1[2]	- time stamp[3]	- mouse x position[4]	- mouse y position[5]	- button state; bitfield with the following entries:		1	-	yellow (e.g., right) button		2	-	blue (e.g., middle) button		4	-	red (e.g., left) button		[all other bits are currently undefined][6]	- modifier keys; bitfield with the following entries:		1	-	shift key		2	-	ctrl key		4	-	(Mac specific) option key		8	-	Cmd/Alt key		[all other bits are currently undefined][7]	- unused[8]	- unusedKeyboard event===================[1]	- event type = 2[2]	- time stamp[3]	- character code		For now the character code is in Mac Roman encoding.[4]	- press state; integer with the following meaning		0	-	character		1	-	key press (down)		2	- 	key release (up)[5]	- modifier keys (same as in mouse events)[6]	- unused[7]	- unused[8]	- unusedFile Drag-Drop event========================[1]	- event type = 3[2]	- time stamp[3]	- subtype	1	- drag enter	2	- drag move	3	- drag leave	4	- file drop	5	- drag to another window[4]	- drop position x[5]	- drop position y[6]	- modifier bits[7]	- file count[8]	- unusedMenu event===============[1]	- event type = 4[2]	- time stamp[3]	- menu ID[4]	- item ID[5]	- unused?[6]	- unused?[7]	- unused?[8]	- window IDWindow event=================[1]	- event type = 5[2]	- time stamp[3]	- window subtype	1	- geometry change; details in fields 4-7	2	- close	3	- iconize	4	- activate	5	- redraw[4]	- window left[5]	- window top[6]	- window width[7]	- window height[8]	- window ID!----STARTUP----(19 February 2009 10:14:19 am) as /Users/jmaloney/Desktop/MIT Squeak/MITBase.image!----SNAPSHOT----(19 February 2009 1:08:03 pm) priorSource: 6648934!Sensor!Sensor useOSEvents: true!events collect: [:e |